  "slug": "quantum-amplification-linear-c32f",
  "summary": "Preprints pair a 546 Hz heralded atom-atom link over 20 km with MDI-QKD, repeater and spin-chain proposals for distributing entanglement.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is entanglement distribution and secure-key generation across separated nodes, with emphasis on reducing resource overhead. Theory proposals include in-memory MDI-QKD, which reports higher key rates and halved memory requirements, and sequential repeater designs in which simple repetition and parity codes outperform unencoded strategies. Measured spin-chain dynamics is proposed for generating pure entangled states between distant qubits in a single channel, while virtual autopurification builds virtual copies from subregions of one translationally invariant system. Experimentally, a 546 Hz heralded atom-atom link over 20 km of fiber uses two 15x15 memory arrays without active phase stabilization, and a three-party frequency-bin secret sharing scheme maintains correlations under 20 MHz pseudorandom basis switching.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
